<h2 id="accessory-drive">Alternator &amp; Power Steering Brackets</h2>
<p>
  There are a handful of alternator and power steering bracket setups you can run. Which one fits depends on the
  <a href="/guides/engine-selection#spacing">LS accessory spacing</a> you go with. Two that work well in a Gen Coupe:
</p>
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Setup</th><th>Spacing</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><a href="https://ictbillet.com/ls-corvette-low-mount-alternator-power-steering-pump-brackets-lsx-ls1-ls3-ls2.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>ICT Billet low mount</strong></a> (551769-1, ~$277–$320)</td>
      <td>Corvette</td>
      <td>Billet bracket for the alternator and power steering pump, with idlers and hardware. Takes an LS truck alternator (5.46" bolt pattern; factory alternators need some block grinding) and a 1998–02 Camaro power steering pump. Iron blocks need extra holes drilled and tapped.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Holley low mount</strong> (alternator / P/S kits like 20-156, A/C version 20-162)</td>
      <td>F-body (middle); truck with spacer kit 21-4</td>
      <td>Complete kits with aluminum brackets, alternator, power steering pump and tensioner, with or without an SD7 A/C compressor. Corvette-spacing engines need the water pump and crank pulley swapped to middle or long spacing.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
